Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:35:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 333/335] Meridian: a CLI's --version is asked with the HOME
 Meridian was given, never in the home folder

agent_cli's Which() asked each copy of Claude Code its --version with
HOME = base::GetHomeDir(), which on macOS asks the system and ignores
HOME, and ran it in that folder. In a test that meant the owner's real
home and folder: the stand-ins refused to run there, neither copy said
its version, and the old one first on the PATH won.

ai::CliHome() is the one home for the person's CLIs: HOME as the process
got it; under the test switches --meridian-test-home, else the test's
HOME, and never the computer's real home (a private empty folder then).
Which(), Connect's config home and the accounts' home use it, as does the
tests' minimal login environment. ai::FindNewestCli() is the newest-copy
lookup every place that starts an agent CLI shares; its --version probes
run in an empty temp folder of their own, with HOME from CliHome() when a
test left the real one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
